From f2eed3642598d4e61449e832d2e9eeff67f73af9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: atomozero <bernardi.andrea@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 22:34:22 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 242/270] tegra_dc: hardware cursor on window C

The Tegra 2 hardware cursor only has two colors, so, as Linux does, the
cursor is window C: a 64x64 B8G8R8A8 image blended over window A with
the alpha of its pixels (window A takes the dependent weight). A cursor
partly off the left or top edge is cropped through the read offsets,
since a window position cannot be negative. Window C gets the same high
priority memory requests as window A.

"hardware_cursor false" in the tegra_dc driver settings leaves the
cursor to app_server.

Signed-off-by: atomozero <bernardi.andrea@gmail.com>
